# Core

Elynd: English **learning space** for adults who struggle to persist—interesting, mostly understandable real content (read + listen); AI/tools lower friction. Not a course, vocab pack, or chatbot. Monorepo: `apps/backend` (Adonis **3333**), `apps/web` (Next **3000**), `packages/shared` (cross-app constants/types; Adonis persistence is Lucid in-app).

Product SSOT: `docs/product/` (vision, philosophy, MVP scope, metrics, decision guide, guardrails). Prototypes: `prd/`.

Language: talk to the user in **Chinese** when they write Chinese; **code, docs, comments, commits in English**.

## Principles

| | |
| --- | --- |
| KISS | Simplest readable solution; early returns |
| YAGNI | No speculative abstractions |
| DRY | Extract only after **three** stabilized uses |
| SSOT | One authority per fact — import/derive, never a parallel copy |
| SRP | One cohesive concern per module/file |
| Fail Fast | Never swallow errors |
| Determinism | Tests deterministic; prefer file-scoped checks |
| Reversibility | Small blast radius |

**SSOT vs DRY:** DRY = when to share a helper (after 3 uses). SSOT = same fact (schema/env/policy/DTO) must not have a second definition — fix the owner or import. Side-effectful owner → fix the export; do not copy.

## Must / Ask / Never

**Must:** follow `layering` + `structure` before adding files/dirs; Lucid schema in `apps/backend/database` / cross-app contracts in `@elynd/shared` before inventing layout; DB schema before consumers; extend root `tsconfig.base.json` via relative paths.

**Ask first** (format: plan → reason → impact → alternative → proceed?):

1. `components/ui/**` (design-system)
2. Root/package config (`package.json`, `tsconfig*`, eslint/prettier, workspace)
3. Deleting files or directories
4. New deps or major bumps
5. Auth method/provider changes
6. Large schema changes affecting existing data

Exceptions: explicit user instruction for that path; obvious one-line bug fix; lint/test/typecheck runs.

**Never:** commit secrets/`.env`; commit local `docker-compose.yaml`; touch `node_modules/`; operate on production data; disable security middleware; start `dev:*`/`start`/`preview` without approval; `apps/web` ↔ `apps/backend` app-source imports; push without approval; write TypeScript imports with `.js`/`.mjs`/`.cjs`/`.jsx` suffixes when the target is a TS/TSX module (use extensionless or `.ts`/`.tsx`; only use `.js` when importing a real JavaScript file).

## Security

No hardcoded secrets; no server secrets in client bundles; validate at boundaries (Zod/Vine); parameterized DB only (Lucid); no production stack traces to clients.

## TDD

Default for behavior-changing API/web logic: failing test → minimal impl → green → refactor. If skipped in-scope, state why.

**Exceptions:** docs/format/rename, minor style UI, tooling config, generated/scaffold, one-off migrations.

**Test data:** never truncate whole tables; delete only IDs this test created; no broad `like`/date-range cleanup; namespace external state.

## Definition of Done

Relevant tests pass; `pnpm lint` / `format:check` / `typecheck` for touched scope; no dead code/dangling imports; explicit errors; no new TODO unless deferred by user.

## Commit (agent)

English imperative; one logical change; prefer subject-only. Format via commitlint — do not restate types here. Review staged diff before commit.

## Intent router

| Intent | Follow |
| --- | --- |
| New API feature on Adonis (`apps/backend`) | `adonis-backend` + `structure` + `layering` (Lucid in-app; Ace `make:*`) |
| Web UI / `features/**` | `frontend` |
| Package / schema ownership | `packages` + `layering` |
| Add/delete/split/move files or dirs | `structure` |
| Where does X belong? | `layering` |
| Product scope / should we build X / drift risk | `docs/product/` (decision guide + guardrails + MVP scope) |

Rule SoT: `.cursor/rules/`. Tooling (ESLint, Prettier, typecheck, tests) wins on conflict. Filled `.trellis/spec` next; filled `docs/product/` for product intent; User Rules last.
